{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1708340,
  "courseSlug": "learn-flutter-dart-to-build-ios-android-apps",
  "courseTitle": "Flutter & Dart - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37215164",
      "title": "Working with the Request & Waiting for the Response",
      "lectureOrder": 228,
      "videoOrder": 212,
      "sourceHash": "086d4f80e65b9249f184b8369eac242a2b9bf7e0904bf537e21faae3027e9a7f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.592,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "So how can we now get our data back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 6.783,
          "en": "from Firebase to our app?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.92,
          "end": 9.93,
          "en": "Well, for that, of course, we wanna go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.93,
          "end": 13.77,
          "en": "to the grocery list screen to this widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.77,
          "end": 17.25,
          "en": "And there we wanna send a get request to Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.25,
          "end": 18.69,
          "en": "because I mentioned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.69,
          "end": 20.47,
          "en": "that in the end, it's such a get request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.47,
          "end": 22.533,
          "en": "that gets you data from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.91,
          "end": 27.12,
          "en": "But before we do that, we have to do one other thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 29.01,
          "en": "We have to make sure that we wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.01,
          "end": 32.013,
          "en": "for this post-request to complete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.013,
          "end": 36.48,
          "en": "Otherwise, if we do go back too early, we might not be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.48,
          "end": 37.603,
          "en": "to fetch the data yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.603,
          "end": 42.21,
          "en": "because it might not have finished sending to Firebase yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.21,
          "end": 44.97,
          "en": "It might not be stored there yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.97,
          "end": 48.84,
          "en": "Because with HTTP requests, you have to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.84,
          "end": 51.653,
          "en": "and keep in mind that they take some time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.653,
          "end": 55.984,
          "en": "not a large amount of time typically, but a few milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.984,
          "end": 59.34,
          "en": "or seconds because after all, a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.34,
          "end": 63.09,
          "en": "must be created, must be sent to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.09,
          "end": 66.94,
          "en": "And the backend then must handle that request, do its work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.94,
          "end": 69.78,
          "en": "for example, store the data in a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.78,
          "end": 74.31,
          "en": "and then the backend needs to create a response, a success",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.31,
          "end": 79.173,
          "en": "or failure response and send back that response to your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.43,
          "end": 83.46000000000001,
          "en": "And in the end, it's this response we wanna wait for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 86.34,
          "en": "because then we know that everything worked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.34,
          "end": 89.01,
          "en": "Or if it failed, we know why it failed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.01,
          "end": 91.95,
          "en": "because we only know whether everything worked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.95,
          "end": 95.968,
          "en": "and that the data was stored once we have that response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.968,
          "end": 99.9,
          "en": "and it's only thereafter that we should try loading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.9,
          "end": 102.93299999999999,
          "en": "or manipulating that data on that server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.07,
          "end": 107.009,
          "en": "So that's therefore the next question, how can we wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.009,
          "end": 109.009,
          "en": "for that response?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.009,
          "end": 113.636,
          "en": "Well, the post-method of this HTTP package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.636,
          "end": 115.83,
          "en": "actually returns some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.83,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "It returns a Future that eventually resolves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 121.308,
          "en": "to a response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.308,
          "end": 126.18,
          "en": "and you learn about futures earlier in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.18,
          "end": 127.357,
          "en": "Futures are these objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.357,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "which will eventually give you access to other data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 135.096,
          "en": "And it makes sense that post yields such a future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.096,
          "end": 138.528,
          "en": "because we don't have a response instantly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.528,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "after executing that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 144.32999999999998,
          "en": "but instead only once the server is done with its work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.32999999999998,
          "end": 146.21699999999998,
          "en": "That's why post gives us a future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.21699999999998,
          "end": 150.243,
          "en": "that will eventually give us access to the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.56,
          "end": 154.149,
          "en": "Now, as you learned earlier, there are two main ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.149,
          "end": 158.313,
          "en": "of getting access to that response data here in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.15,
          "end": 161.37,
          "en": "You can add a then method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.37,
          "end": 163.38,
          "en": "on the result of calling post,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.38,
          "end": 166.2,
          "en": "so chained on the post-method in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.2,
          "end": 168.57,
          "en": "and then you can pass a function to then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.57,
          "end": 171.09,
          "en": "and in here, you would get your response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.09,
          "end": 175.263,
          "en": "and then here, you could work with that response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.12,
          "end": 180.3,
          "en": "Alternatively, since this can be a bit inconvenient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.3,
          "end": 185.1,
          "en": "to write, you can convert saveItem to an async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.1,
          "end": 188.4,
          "en": "by adding the async keyword here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.4,
          "end": 192.78,
          "en": "And this then allows you to await this response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.78,
          "end": 196.5,
          "en": "by adding the await keyword here in front of the method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.5,
          "end": 198.15,
          "en": "that yields the future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.15,
          "end": 201.66,
          "en": "because a weight is meant to be used on futures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.66,
          "end": 203.55,
          "en": "And then with a weight added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.55,
          "end": 207.03,
          "en": "Dart will basically add this then method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.03,
          "end": 211.2,
          "en": "for you invisibly behind the scenes you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 212.79,
          "en": "and it will give you access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.79,
          "end": 214.893,
          "en": "to the response data once it's there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.91,
          "end": 218.1,
          "en": "So then we get our response here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.1,
          "end": 222.51,
          "en": "and we'll wait for this request and response cycle to finish",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.51,
          "end": 224.67000000000002,
          "en": "before this data is available and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 224.67000000000002,
          "end": 228.51,
          "en": "before the next line of code will be executed by dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.51,
          "end": 230.82,
          "en": "And typically, this async await syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.82,
          "end": 234,
          "en": "is a bit more convenient, which is why I'm using this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234,
          "end": 236.13,
          "en": "instead of chaining this then method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.13,
          "end": 239.73,
          "en": "which you could alternatively also do though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.73,
          "end": 243.231,
          "en": "So it's here where we do now have access to this response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.231,
          "end": 246.511,
          "en": "And this response object now has a couple of properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.511,
          "end": 248.76,
          "en": "that can be helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.76,
          "end": 252.3,
          "en": "For example, a statusCode property, which is an integer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.3,
          "end": 256.23,
          "en": "which tells us whether the request succeeded or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.23,
          "end": 259.863,
          "en": "There are some standardized statusCodes you can look for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.863,
          "end": 264.863,
          "en": "For example, 200 or 201 tells you that everything worked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 265.59,
          "end": 269.399,
          "en": "400 ish or 500 ish errors like 404 tell you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 269.399,
          "end": 272.19,
          "en": "that something went wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 272.19,
          "end": 274.83,
          "en": "And you might have seen a 404 error before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.83,
          "end": 278.13,
          "en": "if you visited a website that doesn't exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 278.13,
          "end": 280.11,
          "en": "So this statusCode can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 280.11,
          "end": 282.12,
          "en": "to check whether everything worked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 282.12,
          "end": 283.62,
          "en": "And I'll get back to this later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 283.62,
          "end": 286.3,
          "en": "For the moment, we'll just assume that it worked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.52,
          "end": 290.308,
          "en": "and it then still this response which has a body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 290.308,
          "end": 293.679,
          "en": "with some response data that might have been attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 293.679,
          "end": 297.06,
          "en": "to the response sent back by the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.06,
          "end": 299.49,
          "en": "And it will always depend on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 299.49,
          "end": 303.57,
          "en": "and your server, which exact data is stored in that body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 303.57,
          "end": 305.7,
          "en": "and how it's formatted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 305.7,
          "end": 307.38,
          "en": "In case of Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 309.54,
          "en": "we can take a look at the official documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.54,
          "end": 310.639,
          "en": "to see what's sent back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 310.639,
          "end": 315.27,
          "en": "and we learn that we get back this JSON data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.27,
          "end": 317.1,
          "en": "in a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.1,
          "end": 319.44,
          "en": "This is how JSON data looks like, by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.44,
          "end": 321.87,
          "en": "It looks a lot like a map in Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.87,
          "end": 324.45,
          "en": "And indeed, we can easily convert this back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 324.45,
          "end": 326.55,
          "en": "to a map if we wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 326.55,
          "end": 329.52,
          "en": "So it's this kind of data we get back from the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 329.52,
          "end": 330.78,
          "en": "And in the end, as you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 330.78,
          "end": 334.08,
          "en": "it's simply a key named name which then contains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 334.08,
          "end": 337.8,
          "en": "the unique ID that was generated automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 337.8,
          "end": 339.36,
          "en": "And this can be useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 339.36,
          "end": 342.84000000000003,
          "en": "and this is something we'll use soon for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 342.84000000000003,
          "end": 344.185,
          "en": "I don't care about it though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 344.185,
          "end": 347.713,
          "en": "I only care about the fact that we do wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 347.713,
          "end": 350.04,
          "en": "for the response to be there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 350.04,
          "end": 353.523,
          "en": "And that's what we are doing here thanks to await.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 353.523,
          "end": 357.54,
          "en": "So for the moment here, I'll just print response body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 357.54,
          "end": 359.64,
          "en": "so that we can see it in the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.64,
          "end": 362.043,
          "en": "and I'll print my statusCode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 363,
          "end": 367.653,
          "en": "And with that, we can then pop this screen and go back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 368.58,
          "end": 370.8,
          "en": "Now here, I'm actually getting a warning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 370.8,
          "end": 371.97,
          "en": "that I should not try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 371.97,
          "end": 375.72,
          "en": "to use the build context across async gaps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 375.72,
          "end": 378.63,
          "en": "which simply means after awaiting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 378.63,
          "end": 380.04,
          "en": "because Flutter doesn't know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 380.04,
          "end": 382.819,
          "en": "with certainty whether the context is still the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 382.819,
          "end": 385.2,
          "en": "as before we awaited.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 385.2,
          "end": 388.56,
          "en": "If we, for example, navigated away from this widget here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 388.56,
          "end": 389.39300000000003,
          "en": "in between.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 389.39300000000003,
          "end": 392.61,
          "en": "So whilst the HTTP request was on its way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 392.61,
          "end": 394.714,
          "en": "a context would be referring to a widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 394.714,
          "end": 397.29,
          "en": "that might not be visible anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 397.29,
          "end": 399,
          "en": "That's why it's not recommended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 399,
          "end": 401.64,
          "en": "to use context here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 401.64,
          "end": 403.68,
          "en": "Now, to make sure that we're not referring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
